The primary reason most warlocks are seen with voidwalkers, despite the succubus being a better choice for leveling and questing, is their role in tanking and threat generation. Voidwalkers excel at taunting and generating threat, making them ideal for high-damage encounters where the warlock needs to draw aggro. Succubuses, while powerful in other aspects, are not as effective at this role. [end of text]


